{"userId":"guest","userEmail":"guest@milkanalysis.local","adulterantSlug":"water","adulterantName":"Excessive Water / Neutralizers","imageUrl":"/uploads/strip-1792408900503-162051800.png","sampledColorHex":"#291033","sampledColorRgb":[41,16,51],"detectedStatus":"ADULTERATED","confidenceScore":99,"distanceToPure":76,"distanceToAdulterated":0,"chemicalReport":{"purpose":"Used for volume dilution, which drastically lowers natural density and SNF; neutralizers mask acidity of stale milk.","snfImpact":"Directly drops milk Solids-Not-Fat below the statutory 8.5% (cow) and 9.0% (buffalo) standards.","densityImpact":"Lowers density well below 1.026 g/cm³ (Lactometer reading < 26 at 20°C).","chemicalMechanism":"Freezing point depression shift and Rosolic acid / Phenolphthalein pH indicator reaction with neutralizer alkalis.","healthHazards":["Severe child and maternal malnutrition due to diluted protein and calcium","Waterborne pathogens: Salmonella, E. coli, cholera, and Amoebiasis from contaminated tap or pond water","Heavy metal poisoning (lead, arsenic) from untreated water sources","Disruption of stomach acid balance by caustic alkaline neutralizers"],"fssaiLimit":"Added water must be 0%. Lactometer reading must not fall below 28 for cow milk and 30 for buffalo milk."},"notes":"","sampleName":"Milk Sample","createdAt":{"$$date":1792408900512},"_id":"iUJmUuAx8jzTgTOY"}
